# DO Manager API and Backend Conventions

## Context
- This rule applies to all API route handlers and backend code
- Project uses Next.js 15 App Router pattern for API routes
- API routes follow RESTful conventions

## Requirements
- Follow Next.js 15 Route Handlers API patterns
- Implement proper error handling and status codes
- Validate request data using TypeScript types
- Organize route handlers by resource type
- Follow consistent response formats

## API Route Structure
- Place API routes in `src/app/api` directory following Next.js 15 route convention
- Group related endpoints by resource (e.g., `/api/buckets/[id]/route.ts`)
- Use TypeScript interfaces for request and response types
- Implement proper validation for request parameters

## Error Handling
- Use proper HTTP status codes for all responses
- Return consistent error response format
- Include informative error messages for client
- Log detailed errors on server-side
- Implement try/catch blocks for async operations

## Data Validation
- Validate all request parameters and body
- Use TypeScript interfaces for validation
- Return appropriate error responses for invalid data
- Sanitize user input before processing

## Examples
<example>
// Good API route example
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from 'next/server';
import { db } from '@/lib/db';
import { BucketFormData } from '@/types/bucket';

export async function POST(request: NextRequest) {
  try {
    const data = await request.json() as BucketFormData;
    
    // Validate required fields
    if (!data.name) {
      return NextResponse.json(
        { error: 'Name is required' },
        { status: 400 }
      );
    }
    
    const bucket = await db.bucket.create({
      data: {
        name: data.name,
        description: data.description,
        ownerId: 'user-id', // In real code, get from auth
      },
    });
    
    return NextResponse.json(bucket, { status: 201 });
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error creating bucket:', error);
    return NextResponse.json(
      { error: 'Failed to create bucket' },
      { status: 500 }
    );
  }
}
</example>

